    "result_text": "The build passes and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented a derived `timezone` field on the owner representation, mapping the locality/region to an IANA timezone name via the fixed table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane).\n\nChanges:\n- **`LocalityResolver.java`** \u2014 added a `REGION_TIMEZONE` table and a public `timezone(String region)` method that returns the IANA name for a region, or `null` when the region is `null`/unknown.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 extracted the existing locality derivation into a `locality(owner)` helper (customer-code REGION segment, else postcode/city resolution), reused it for the `locality` mapping, and added a new `timezone` mapping that feeds that same region into `LocalityResolver.timezone(...)`. This keeps `timezone` consistent with the reported `locality`.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` string property to the owner schema (the DTO is generated from this spec), documenting the region-to-timezone derivation.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` (Sydney \u2192 NSW \u2192 `Australia/Sydney`) passes, along with the rest of the suite.",
